/**
 * A recording of a real hotel room, as base64 AAC.
 *
 * It lives in a JavaScript module rather than as an audio file because the
 * frontend deploy filters what it uploads by extension, and no audio or video
 * type is on that list — the same reason landingpage-hero.mp4 and the
 * notification tones do not load on stage. A .js file always ships, so the bed
 * travels with the code that plays it.
 *
 * Imported dynamically by ReservationVoice, so webpack emits it as its own
 * chunk and only the voice page pays for it.
 *
 * Revert to a plain asset once the deploy carries media. To get the audio back:
 *   node -e "require('fs').writeFileSync('a.m4a',Buffer.from(require('./src/assets/hotel-ambience').default,'base64'))"
 *
 * 24kHz mono, ~32s, cut from the middle of a longer recording and levelled in
 * the browser to RESERVATION_VOICE_AMBIENCE_DBFS.
 */
export default '';
